use "emit_c.a0"

# A0 port of the instruction-list post-processing `Code.finish` of src/wasm.ts (DESIGN.md 7a): the
# function body arrives as a list of instructions with SYMBOLIC local indices; `wfzfin` stackifies
# adjacent local.set/local.get pairs, drops dead stores, renumbers the non-parameter locals so that
# ones with disjoint live ranges (widened across loops) share an index, and serializes the list.
# The result is byte-identical to the TypeScript (compiler/wasm_code.a0 is checked against `finish`
# on random lists and on every function body of the test programs).
#
# Input: the table `ins` (u32x128x352: 22528 instructions of 2 words; instruction k is word 2k =
# kind, word 2k+1 = v), the instruction count n and the parameter count np (locals below np are
# never renumbered or removed). The kinds, and the bytes each serializes to (uleb/sleb are the
# LEB128 forms of src/wasm.ts, sleb of the int32 whose bit pattern is v):
#    0 NOP nothing           1 OP v the byte v&255      2 CONST v 0x41 sleb(v)
#    3 LGET v 0x20 uleb(v)   4 LSET v 0x21 uleb(v)      5 LTEE v 0x22 uleb(v)   (v renumbered below np)
#    6 CALL v: one marker word v (>= 256)               7 POOL v: one marker word 2^31 + v
#    8 LOOP 0x03 0x40        9 LOOPEND 0x0b             10 LOAD v 0x28 2 uleb(v)  11 STORE v 0x36 2 uleb(v)
#   12 BRIF v 0x0d uleb(v)  13 BR v 0x0c uleb(v)        14 BLOCK v 0x02 v&255     15 IF v 0x04 v&255
#   16 MEMCOPY 0xfc 0x0a 0 0  17 MEMFILL 0xfc 0x0b 0    18 SIMD v 0xfd uleb(v)    19 VSTORE 0xfd 0x0b 2 0
#   20 VCONSTIDX 0xfd 0x0c then the lanes 0 1 2 3 (u32, little endian)
#   21 VCONSTSPLAT v 0xfd 0x0c then v (little endian) four times
#   22 GGET v 0x23 v&255    23 GSET v 0x24 v&255
# A local id below 2^20 (VBASE) is an i32 local (id < 8192 when not a parameter), an id VBASE + k
# (k < 128) a v128 local; the v128 locals are placed after the i32 ones. A local id outside these
# ranges, more than 22528 instructions, or more than 65533 output words is the failure value.
# Loops (kinds 8, 9) are balanced and nested; blocks and ifs are not loops.
#
# Result (wfzfin): the code table (u32x128x512). Words 0 .. nwords-1 are the body, one word per
# byte plus a marker word for each CALL/POOL; the last three words are the header: word 65533 =
# nwords, the number of words written (4294967295 on failure, then the other two are 0), word
# 65534 = nlocals (the i32 locals above the np parameters) and word 65535 = nvlocals (the v128
# locals), i.e. `locals` and `vlocals` of `Code.finish`. (A record with the table would pass
# the 2^21 bit limit of a value, so the three scalars live in the table: the body holds at most
# 65533 words.)
#
# Method. Every pass is a fold over the instructions whose state is a table (u32x128x512 = 65536
# words, element i at page i>>7, word i&127), updated in place; tables read by a pass are fold
# extras (borrowed, never copied), and a write is a one-trip fold of a tiny body (`wfzp1`, ...).
# 1. wfzcnt: gets and sets per local (a LTEE counts as a set) over the original list.
# 2. wfzstk: stackify on a copy of the list: a set directly followed by a get of the same local
#    vanishes with it (one read, one write) or becomes a tee; a dead set becomes OP 0x1a, a dead
#    tee vanishes. A removed instruction is kind 0; positions stay the original indices.
# 3. wfzrng: per local its first and last access and the top-level (outermost) loop around each;
#    per top-level loop its start and end. Since loops nest, repeated widening against all loops
#    is the hull with the outermost loop around the first access (start) and last access (end).
# 4. wfzalc: the locals in order of first access (the TypeScript stable sort by widened start gives
#    the same order) take the first slot whose end is below the widened start; i32 and v128 locals
#    have separate slot sets; the slot is kept per local.
# 5. wfzoff, wfzcode: the offset of every instruction (running sum of its length), then its
#    bytes, written one by one (wfzbyte).
# The tables start as `wfzz` (all zero) and are laid out as follows (word indices):
#   count table  : gets of local c at c, sets at 8320 + c (c: i32 id, or 8192 + k for VBASE + k),
#                  16640: set to 1 when a local id is out of range, 16641 scratch
#   range table  : 0 loop depth, 1 top-level loop count, 8 9 16..19 scratch, 128 + 4c: first
#                  access + 1, its top-level loop, last access, its top-level loop,
#                  33408 + L: start and 44928 + L: end of top-level loop L
#   slot table   : c: slot of local c, 8320 + s: end of i32 slot s, 16512 + s: end of v128 slot
#                  s, 16640 and 16641: slots used (i32, v128), 16650 and 16651 scratch
#   offset table : word i is the offset of instruction i (n + 1 words)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tables

# word p1 of the table p0
fn wfzg u32x128x512 u32 -> u32
pi shr p1 7
pg get p0 pi
w and p1 127
v get pg w
ret v
end
# word p1 of the input list
fn wfzgi u32x128x352 u32 -> u32
pi shr p1 7
pg get p0 pi
w and p1 127
v get pg w
ret v
end
# the state with word p2 set to p3 (a fold of one trip: p1 is the trip)
fn wfzp1 u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
pi shr p2 7
pg get p0 pi
w and p2 127
pg2 set pg w p3
t set p0 pi pg2
ret t
end
# the state with the words p2 and p2 + 1 (same page) set to p3 and p4
fn wfzp2 u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
pi shr p2 7
pg get p0 pi
w and p2 127
pg2 set pg w p3
w1 add w 1
pg3 set pg2 w1 p4
t set p0 pi pg3
ret t
end
# the state with the words p2 .. p2 + 3 (p2 a multiple of 4) set to p3 .. p6
fn wfzp4 u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
pi shr p2 7
pg get p0 pi
w and p2 127
pg2 set pg w p3
w1 add w 1
pg3 set pg2 w1 p4
w2 add w 2
pg4 set pg3 w2 p5
w3 add w 3
pg5 set pg4 w3 p6
t set p0 pi pg5
ret t
end
# the zero table
fn wfzz -> u32x128x512
z call zpage
t arr z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z
ret t
end
# the zero input list
fn wfzzi -> u32x128x352
z call zpage
t arr z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z z
ret t
end
# page p1 of the input list p2 copied into the state (a fold of 352 trips)
fn wfzcp u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x352 -> u32x128x512
pg get p2 p1
t set p0 p1 pg
ret t
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local ids

# 1 for a local access kind (3 get, 4 set, 5 tee)
fn wfzisl u32 -> bool
d sub p0 3
r lt d 3
ret r
end
# the compact index of local id p0: i32 ids below 8192 as they are, VBASE + k (k < 128) as 8192 + k,
# 0 for an id out of range
fn wfzcidx u32 -> u32
lo lt p0 8192
vv sub p0 1048576
vl lt vv 128
vi add vv 8192
a select vl vi 0
c select lo p0 a
ret c
end
# is local id p0 in range
fn wfzvok u32 -> bool
lo lt p0 8192
vv sub p0 1048576
vl lt vv 128
r or lo vl
ret r
end
# the final index of local id p0 (slot table p0, parameters p1, i32 locals p2): parameters stay,
# an i32 local is np + slot, a v128 local np + nl + slot
fn wfzmap u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 -> u32
c call wfzcidx p3
a call wfzg p0 c
lo lt p3 8192
isp lt p3 p1
q add p1 a
nl add p1 p2
qv add nl a
r0 select lo q qv
r select isp p3 r0
ret r
end
# the operand of an instruction after renumbering: the final index for a local access (kind p3,
# value p4), else p4
fn wfzuse u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32
isl call wfzisl p3
m call wfzmap p0 p1 p2 p4
r select isl m p4
ret r
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bytes

# bytes of the uleb128 form of p0 (1..5)
fn wfzul u32 -> u32
a ge p0 128
b ge p0 16384
c ge p0 2097152
d ge p0 268435456
ai select a 1 0
bi select b 1 0
ci select c 1 0
di select d 1 0
s1 add ai bi
s2 add s1 ci
s3 add s2 di
r add s3 1
ret r
end
# bytes of the sleb128 form of the int32 with the bit pattern p0 (1..5)
fn wfzsl u32 -> u32
x1 add p0 64
x2 add p0 8192
x3 add p0 1048576
x4 add p0 134217728
a ge x1 128
b ge x2 16384
c ge x3 2097152
d ge x4 268435456
ai select a 1 0
bi select b 1 0
ci select c 1 0
di select d 1 0
s1 add ai bi
s2 add s1 ci
s3 add s2 di
r add s3 1
ret r
end
# byte p1 of the uleb128 form of p0
fn wfzuleb u32 u32 -> u32
len call wfzul p0
m1 add p1 1
cont lt m1 len
sh mul p1 7
x shr p0 sh
b and x 127
b8 or b 128
r select cont b8 b
ret r
end
# byte p1 of the sleb128 form of the int32 with the bit pattern p0
fn wfzsleb u32 u32 -> u32
len call wfzsl p0
m1 add p1 1
cont lt m1 len
sh mul p1 7
x shr p0 sh
sg shr p0 31
neg eq sg 1
shp gt sh 0
ng and neg shp
rs sub 32 sh
ones shl 4294967295 rs
ext select ng ones 0
y or x ext
b and y 127
b8 or b 128
r select cont b8 b
ret r
end
# length of the fixed prefix of kind p0
fn wfzplen u32 -> u32
qd mov 0
qe2 eq p0 2
qr2 select qe2 1 qd
qe3 eq p0 3
qr3 select qe3 1 qr2
qe4 eq p0 4
qr4 select qe4 1 qr3
qe5 eq p0 5
qr5 select qe5 1 qr4
qe8 eq p0 8
qr8 select qe8 2 qr5
qe9 eq p0 9
qr9 select qe9 1 qr8
qe10 eq p0 10
qr10 select qe10 2 qr9
qe11 eq p0 11
qr11 select qe11 2 qr10
qe12 eq p0 12
qr12 select qe12 1 qr11
qe13 eq p0 13
qr13 select qe13 1 qr12
qe14 eq p0 14
qr14 select qe14 1 qr13
qe15 eq p0 15
qr15 select qe15 1 qr14
qe16 eq p0 16
qr16 select qe16 4 qr15
qe17 eq p0 17
qr17 select qe17 3 qr16
qe18 eq p0 18
qr18 select qe18 1 qr17
qe19 eq p0 19
qr19 select qe19 4 qr18
qe20 eq p0 20
qr20 select qe20 2 qr19
qe21 eq p0 21
qr21 select qe21 2 qr20
qe22 eq p0 22
qr22 select qe22 1 qr21
qe23 eq p0 23
qr23 select qe23 1 qr22
ret qr23
end
# the fixed prefix bytes of kind p0, packed little endian
fn wfzpack u32 -> u32
qd mov 0
qe2 eq p0 2
qr2 select qe2 65 qd
qe3 eq p0 3
qr3 select qe3 32 qr2
qe4 eq p0 4
qr4 select qe4 33 qr3
qe5 eq p0 5
qr5 select qe5 34 qr4
qe8 eq p0 8
qr8 select qe8 16387 qr5
qe9 eq p0 9
qr9 select qe9 11 qr8
qe10 eq p0 10
qr10 select qe10 552 qr9
qe11 eq p0 11
qr11 select qe11 566 qr10
qe12 eq p0 12
qr12 select qe12 13 qr11
qe13 eq p0 13
qr13 select qe13 12 qr12
qe14 eq p0 14
qr14 select qe14 2 qr13
qe15 eq p0 15
qr15 select qe15 4 qr14
qe16 eq p0 16
qr16 select qe16 2812 qr15
qe17 eq p0 17
qr17 select qe17 3068 qr16
qe18 eq p0 18
qr18 select qe18 253 qr17
qe19 eq p0 19
qr19 select qe19 134141 qr18
qe20 eq p0 20
qr20 select qe20 3325 qr19
qe21 eq p0 21
qr21 select qe21 3325 qr20
qe22 eq p0 22
qr22 select qe22 35 qr21
qe23 eq p0 23
qr23 select qe23 36 qr22
ret qr23
end
# length of the variable part of kind p0 whose operand is p1
fn wfzvlen u32 u32 -> u32
ul call wfzul p1
sl call wfzsl p1
qd mov 0
qe1 eq p0 1
qr1 select qe1 1 qd
qe2 eq p0 2
qr2 select qe2 sl qr1
qe3 eq p0 3
qr3 select qe3 ul qr2
qe4 eq p0 4
qr4 select qe4 ul qr3
qe5 eq p0 5
qr5 select qe5 ul qr4
qe6 eq p0 6
qr6 select qe6 1 qr5
qe7 eq p0 7
qr7 select qe7 1 qr6
qe10 eq p0 10
qr10 select qe10 ul qr7
qe11 eq p0 11
qr11 select qe11 ul qr10
qe12 eq p0 12
qr12 select qe12 ul qr11
qe13 eq p0 13
qr13 select qe13 ul qr12
qe14 eq p0 14
qr14 select qe14 1 qr13
qe15 eq p0 15
qr15 select qe15 1 qr14
qe18 eq p0 18
qr18 select qe18 ul qr15
qe20 eq p0 20
qr20 select qe20 16 qr18
qe21 eq p0 21
qr21 select qe21 16 qr20
qe22 eq p0 22
qr22 select qe22 1 qr21
qe23 eq p0 23
qr23 select qe23 1 qr22
ret qr23
end
# words of the instruction of kind p0 with operand p1 (a local access: its final index)
fn wfzlen u32 u32 -> u32
a call wfzplen p0
b call wfzvlen p0 p1
r add a b
ret r
end
# the variable byte p2 of kind p0 with operand p1 (the index counts from the end of the prefix)
fn wfzvar u32 u32 u32 -> u32
ulb call wfzuleb p1 p2
slb call wfzsleb p1 p2
u8 and p1 255
m3 and p2 3
sh mul m3 8
xs shr p1 sh
bv and xs 255
l0 eq m3 0
ln shr p2 2
lane select l0 ln 0
mk add p1 2147483648
qd mov 0
qe1 eq p0 1
qr1 select qe1 u8 qd
qe2 eq p0 2
qr2 select qe2 slb qr1
qe3 eq p0 3
qr3 select qe3 ulb qr2
qe4 eq p0 4
qr4 select qe4 ulb qr3
qe5 eq p0 5
qr5 select qe5 ulb qr4
qe6 eq p0 6
qr6 select qe6 p1 qr5
qe7 eq p0 7
qr7 select qe7 mk qr6
qe10 eq p0 10
qr10 select qe10 ulb qr7
qe11 eq p0 11
qr11 select qe11 ulb qr10
qe12 eq p0 12
qr12 select qe12 ulb qr11
qe13 eq p0 13
qr13 select qe13 ulb qr12
qe14 eq p0 14
qr14 select qe14 u8 qr13
qe15 eq p0 15
qr15 select qe15 u8 qr14
qe18 eq p0 18
qr18 select qe18 ulb qr15
qe20 eq p0 20
qr20 select qe20 lane qr18
qe21 eq p0 21
qr21 select qe21 bv qr20
qe22 eq p0 22
qr22 select qe22 u8 qr21
qe23 eq p0 23
qr23 select qe23 u8 qr22
ret qr23
end
# word p2 of the instruction of kind p0 with operand p1: a byte, or a marker for a call or a pool address
fn wfzbyte u32 u32 u32 -> u32
pl call wfzplen p0
pk call wfzpack p0
inp lt p2 pl
j8 mul p2 8
x shr pk j8
pb and x 255
m sub p2 pl
v call wfzvar p0 p1 m
r select inp pb v
ret r
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pass 1: counts. State: the count table; trip i: instruction i of p2 (n = p4, np = p3).

# a get of a local adds one to its gets, a set or tee to its sets
fn wfzcnt u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x352 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
w2 shl p1 1
k call wfzgi p2 w2
w3 add w2 1
v call wfzgi p2 w3
isl call wfzisl k
big ge v p3
inr lt p1 p4
a0 and isl big
act and a0 inr
c call wfzcidx v
ok call wfzvok v
is3 eq k 3
c8 add c 8320
slot select is3 c c8
good and act ok
inc select good 1 0
old call wfzg p0 slot
new add old inc
nok eq ok false
bad and act nok
ft select bad 16640 16641
t1 fold wfzp1 1 p0 slot new
t2 fold wfzp1 1 t1 ft 1
ret t2
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pass 2: stackify. State: the copy of the list; extras: the count table, np, n.

# instruction p1: a set directly followed by a get of the same local (original adjacency) becomes
# nothing together with the get when the local has one get and one set, else a tee; a set whose
# local is never read is OP 0x1a (drop); a tee whose local is never read vanishes. Parameters
# are untouched. A removed instruction is kind 0.
fn wfzstk u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
w2 shl p1 1
k call wfzg p0 w2
w3 add w2 1
v call wfzg p0 w3
w4 add w2 2
nk call wfzg p0 w4
w5 add w2 3
nv call wfzg p0 w5
isl call wfzisl k
big ge v p3
inr lt p1 p4
a0 and isl big
act and a0 inr
c call wfzcidx v
c8 add c 8320
rd call wfzg p2 c
st call wfzg p2 c8
i1 add p1 1
inr1 lt i1 p4
n3 eq nk 3
nvs eq nv v
f0 and n3 nvs
fol and f0 inr1
is4 eq k 4
is5 eq k 5
rd1 eq rd 1
st1 eq st 1
b1 and rd1 st1
rd0 eq rd 0
k4f select b1 0 5
k4n select rd0 1 4
k4 select fol k4f k4n
vd select rd0 26 v
v4 select fol v vd
k5 select rd0 0 5
k50 select is5 k5 k
nk0 select is4 k4 k50
nv0 select is4 v4 v
newk select act nk0 k
newv select act nv0 v
kl0 and act is4
kill and kl0 fol
kv select kill 0 nk
t1 fold wfzp2 1 p0 w2 newk newv
t2 fold wfzp1 1 t1 w4 kv
ret t2
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pass 3: ranges. State: the range table; extras: the stackified list, np.

# instruction p1: loop depth and top-level loops; first and last access of a local
fn wfzrng u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x512 u32 -> u32x128x512
w2 shl p1 1
k call wfzg p2 w2
w3 add w2 1
v call wfzg p2 w3
d call wfzg p0 0
lc call wfzg p0 1
isop eq k 8
iscl eq k 9
d0 eq d 0
topop and isop d0
topi select topop 1 0
lc2 add lc topi
d1 eq d 1
topcl and iscl d1
dinc add d 1
ddec sub d 1
dcl select iscl ddec d
d2 select isop dinc dcl
dpos gt d 0
cur select dpos lc2 0
isl call wfzisl k
big ge v p3
act and isl big
c call wfzcidx v
c4 mul c 4
b4 add c4 128
f call wfzg p0 b4
b41 add b4 1
tf0 call wfzg p0 b41
isf eq f 0
ip1 add p1 1
a0w select isf ip1 f
a1w select isf cur tf0
tg4 select act b4 16
lsi add lc2 33408
lst select topop lsi 8
lei add lc 44928
lex select topcl lei 9
t1 fold wfzp4 1 p0 tg4 a0w a1w p1 cur
t2 fold wfzp2 1 t1 0 d2 lc2
t3 fold wfzp1 1 t2 lst p1
t4 fold wfzp1 1 t3 lex p1
ret t4
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pass 4: slots. State: the slot table; extras: the stackified list, the range table, np.

# slot candidate p0 after slot p1 of the slot table p2 (slot ends from p3 on): the first slot whose
# end is below the start p4, 4294967295 for none yet
fn wfzfit u32 u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32 -> u32
ix add p3 p1
e call wfzg p2 ix
fr lt e p4
nf eq p0 4294967295
tk and fr nf
r select tk p1 p0
ret r
end
# instruction p1: at the first access of a local, give it the first free slot of its kind
fn wfzalc u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x512 u32x128x512 u32 -> u32x128x512
w2 shl p1 1
k call wfzg p2 w2
w3 add w2 1
v call wfzg p2 w3
isl call wfzisl k
big ge v p4
act and isl big
c call wfzcidx v
c4 mul c 4
b4 add c4 128
f call wfzg p3 b4
b41 add b4 1
tlf call wfzg p3 b41
b42 add b4 2
last call wfzg p3 b42
b43 add b4 3
tll call wfzg p3 b43
ip1 add p1 1
fe eq f ip1
isf and act fe
tz eq tlf 0
lsi add tlf 33408
lsv call wfzg p3 lsi
st select tz p1 lsv
ez eq tll 0
lei add tll 44928
lev call wfzg p3 lei
en select ez last lev
lo lt v 8192
sbase select lo 8320 16512
cnti select lo 16640 16641
cnt call wfzg p0 cnti
fit fold wfzfit cnt 4294967295 p0 sbase st
nf eq fit 4294967295
slot select nf cnt fit
inc select nf 1 0
cnt2 add cnt inc
cnt3 select isf cnt2 cnt
ta select isf c 16650
sl2 add sbase slot
te select isf sl2 16651
t1 fold wfzp1 1 p0 ta slot
t2 fold wfzp1 1 t1 te en
t3 fold wfzp1 1 t2 cnti cnt3
ret t3
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pass 5: offsets and bytes

# state: the offset table; instruction p1 of the stackified list p2 starts at word p1 of the
# state, the next at the sum with its length (slot table p3, np p4, i32 locals p5)
fn wfzoff u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x512 u32x128x512 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
w2 shl p1 1
k call wfzg p2 w2
w3 add w2 1
v call wfzg p2 w3
u call wfzuse p3 p4 p5 k v
ln call wfzlen k u
o call wfzg p0 p1
no add o ln
ip1 add p1 1
t fold wfzp1 1 p0 ip1 no
ret t
end
# state: the code table; trip p1 writes word p2 + p1 (the instruction starts at word p2) when p1 is
# below the length p5 of the instruction of kind p3 and operand p4 (a fold of 18 trips: the longest
# instruction is 18 words)
fn wfzbw u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
ix add p2 p1
old call wfzg p0 ix
b call wfzbyte p3 p4 p1
act lt p1 p5
val select act b old
t fold wfzp1 1 p0 ix val
ret t
end
# state: the code table; instruction p1 of the stackified list p2 (slot table p3, offsets p4, np
# p5, i32 locals p6) written at its offset
fn wfzcode u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x512 u32x128x512 u32x128x512 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
w2 shl p1 1
k call wfzg p2 w2
w3 add w2 1
v call wfzg p2 w3
u call wfzuse p3 p5 p6 k v
ln call wfzlen k u
base call wfzg p4 p1
t fold wfzbw 18 p0 base k u ln
ret t
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The function

# `Code.finish(np)` of the list p0 of p1 instructions: the code table, whose last three words
# 65533, 65534, 65535 are the words written (4294967295 on failure), the i32 locals and the v128 locals
fn wfzfin u32x128x352 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
over gt p1 22528
nn select over 22528 p1
z0 call wfzz
stk fold wfzcp 352 z0 p0
zc call wfzz
cnt fold wfzcnt nn zc p0 p2 nn
zr call wfzz
stk2 fold wfzstk nn stk cnt p2 nn
rng fold wfzrng nn zr stk2 p2
zs call wfzz
sa fold wfzalc nn zs stk2 rng p2
nl call wfzg sa 16640
nv call wfzg sa 16641
zo call wfzz
off fold wfzoff nn zo stk2 sa p2 nl
zout call wfzz
cod fold wfzcode nn zout stk2 sa off p2 nl
total call wfzg off nn
flag call wfzg cnt 16640
f0 eq flag 0
fits le total 65533
g1 and f0 fits
nover eq over false
ok and g1 nover
nw select ok total 4294967295
nl2 select ok nl 0
nv2 select ok nv 0
r1 fold wfzp1 1 cod 65533 nw
r2 fold wfzp1 1 r1 65534 nl2
r3 fold wfzp1 1 r2 65535 nv2
ret r3
end
